 "note": "In the ledger, `sources` holds indices into `sources` below, and method fields hold indices into `methods`.",
 "methods": [
  "Use the already-archived, SHA-256 verified independent NLSC VILLAGE_NLSC_1150817 raw polygons, not the blocked TGOS township download. Recompute every current row and own-item point with raw shapefile parts and odd-even ring crossings; an STRtree indexes only bounding boxes. No boundary repair, coordinate transformation or point movement. The code/node membership comes from the raw official attributes. Empty or conflicting containment remains held.",
  "Use only the literal own Wikidata item and current reference-date P31/P131/P5020 claims. Require a unique official code, compatible existing type/type_local/level, native name, same stored state, consistent non-null parent_id, and exact stored point and own-item point inside raw official August 2026 village geometry of that unit. Administrative city units may aggregate all and only their official township codes; never substitute the central district or a seat.",
  "Country gate precedes count use. Taiwan agency declaration names OGDL 1.0; its clause 4.2 explicitly states CC BY 4.0 compatibility. KR table-specific compatible KOGL not established; RS and CY only unnamed attribution permission: hold licence, exception is owner decision. MT HTTP 403 prevents licence/count verification: hold access without workaround.",
  "Consult the pinned unresolved baseline plus later identity events. For a changed unresolved key require identical v4.0 own item, name/native, administrative type, stored state and exact original point; the independently verified own official unit binding then establishes the same original entity. Changed county-to-seat own items remain held. Emit an ordinary reviewed classification event with unequal current before/after hashes, event_pr 0 and the compact ledger SHA-256; never decision_only.",
  "MOI household-registration table ODRP013, latest advertised period 11509 (2026-09-30), as captured 2026-10-23. All four pages (7,781 unique village codes) exhaustively captured; each people_total equals male+female. Sum only villages with the exact eight-digit own township code, or every township of the own five-digit city-unit code. Official township names and county names/codes reconcile one-to-one with all 368 codes in the national boundary archive. No newer stored-year value or own-item dated claim matching the stored population is replaced.",
  "Change only population and population_year; preserve every other field and row. Exact changed-file bytes, canonical row hashes and scalar presence/value/type guards apply before any write. Only files actually written are guarded; a later master with byte-identical guarded inputs is accepted."
 ],
